Id: ssh027i
Severity: INFO
Category: ssh
Check: check_ssh
Fix: Set UseDNS no (the default) once nothing relies on host-name matching.
References: sshd_config(5)
Controls: CIS 4.1, 5.4; NIST AC-17, IA-2; ISO 8.5, 8.20; CE Secure configuration, User access control

UseDNS is yes: sshd looks up the host name of every connecting address
and checks that it resolves back, so each login waits for the resolver
and connections stall when it is slow or down. With yes, host names may
be matched in authorized_keys from= patterns and in Match Host blocks,
and a name is only as trustworthy as the DNS that answered; with no
(the default since OpenSSH 6.8, and what every distribution ships) only
addresses are matched. A yes was set on purpose: make sure nothing
depends on host-name matching, then set it back.
